2488-130870-0001 V:0.5032 A:0.5065 D:0.5697 HANGING FROM ITS WALLS A DOZEN DIVING OUTFITS WERE WAITING FOR ANYBODY WHO WANTED TO TAKE A STROLL
2488-130870-0002 V:0.4895 A:0.4307 D:0.5484 AFTER SEEING THESE NED LAND EXHIBITED AN OBVIOUS DISTASTE FOR THE IDEA OF PUTTING ONE ON
2488-130870-0003 V:0.5425 A:0.4528 D:0.5478 BUT MY GALLANT NED I TOLD HIM THE FORESTS OF CRESPO ISLAND ARE SIMPLY UNDERWATER FORESTS
2488-130870-0005 V:0.4301 A:0.4331 D:0.5205 PUT IN THE DISAPPOINTED HARPOONER WATCHING HIS DREAMS OF FRESH MEAT FADE AWAY
2488-130870-0006 V:0.4003 A:0.5915 D:0.6640 AND YOU PROFESSOR ARONNAX ARE YOU GOING TO STICK YOURSELF INSIDE THESE CLOTHES
2488-130870-0007 V:0.4357 A:0.4088 D:0.4928 IT HAS TO BE MISTER NED
2488-130870-0008 V:0.3364 A:0.5130 D:0.6022 HAVE IT YOUR WAY SIR THE HARPOONER REPLIED SHRUGGING HIS SHOULDERS BUT SPEAKING FOR MYSELF ILL NEVER GET INTO THOSE THINGS UNLESS THEY FORCE ME
2488-130870-0009 V:0.3001 A:0.3881 D:0.4981 NO ONE WILL FORCE YOU MISTER LAND CAPTAIN NEMO SAID
2488-130870-0010 V:0.3358 A:0.4376 D:0.5292 AND IS CONSEIL GOING TO RISK IT
2488-130870-0011 V:0.3712 A:0.3552 D:0.4260 NED ASKED
2488-130870-0012 V:0.3975 A:0.4075 D:0.4926 WHERE MASTER GOES I GO CONSEIL REPLIED
2488-130870-0013 V:0.5107 A:0.4961 D:0.5800 AT THE CAPTAINS SUMMONS TWO CREWMEN CAME TO HELP US PUT ON THESE HEAVY WATERPROOF CLOTHES MADE FROM SEAMLESS INDIA RUBBER AND EXPRESSLY DESIGNED TO BEAR CONSIDERABLE PRESSURES
2488-130870-0014 V:0.4781 A:0.4483 D:0.5454 THEY WERE LIKE SUITS OF ARMOR THAT WERE BOTH YIELDING AND RESISTANT YOU MIGHT SAY
2488-130870-0015 V:0.4630 A:0.4605 D:0.5567 THESE CLOTHES CONSISTED OF JACKET AND PANTS
2488-130870-0016 V:0.4922 A:0.4611 D:0.5537 THE FABRIC OF THE JACKET WAS REINFORCED WITH COPPER MAIL THAT SHIELDED THE CHEST PROTECTED IT FROM THE WATERS PRESSURE AND ALLOWED THE LUNGS TO FUNCTION FREELY THE SLEEVES ENDED IN SUPPLE GLOVES THAT DIDNT IMPEDE HAND MOVEMENTS
2488-130870-0017 V:0.5446 A:0.5050 D:0.5884 THESE PERFECTED DIVING SUITS IT WAS EASY TO SEE WERE A FAR CRY FROM SUCH MISSHAPEN COSTUMES AS THE CORK BREASTPLATES LEATHER JUMPERS SEAGOING TUNICS INVENTED AND ACCLAIMED IN THE EIGHTEENTH CENTURY
2488-130870-0018 V:0.4908 A:0.4309 D:0.5262 CONSEIL AND I WERE SOON DRESSED IN THESE DIVING SUITS
2488-130870-0019 V:0.5323 A:0.4677 D:0.5532 ALL THAT REMAINED WAS TO ENCASE ONES HEAD IN ITS METAL SPHERE
2488-130870-0020 V:0.4991 A:0.4980 D:0.5753 BUT BEFORE PROCEEDING WITH THIS OPERATION I ASKED THE CAPTAIN FOR PERMISSION TO EXAMINE THE RIFLES SET ASIDE FOR US
2488-130870-0021 V:0.5539 A:0.4807 D:0.5698 ONE OF THE NAUTILUSS MEN PRESENTED ME WITH A STREAMLINED RIFLE WHOSE BUTT WAS BOILERPLATE STEEL HOLLOW INSIDE AND OF FAIRLY LARGE DIMENSIONS
2488-130870-0022 V:0.5421 A:0.5079 D:0.5628 THIS SERVED AS A TANK FOR THE COMPRESSED AIR WHICH A TRIGGER OPERATED VALVE COULD RELEASE INTO THE METAL CHAMBER
2488-130870-0023 V:0.4788 A:0.4913 D:0.5654 IN A GROOVE WHERE THE BUTT WAS HEAVIEST A CARTRIDGE CLIP HELD SOME TWENTY ELECTRIC BULLETS THAT BY MEANS OF A SPRING AUTOMATICALLY TOOK THEIR PLACES IN THE BARREL OF THE RIFLE
2488-130870-0024 V:0.4422 A:0.4818 D:0.5714 AS SOON AS ONE SHOT HAD BEEN FIRED ANOTHER WAS READY TO GO OFF
2488-130870-0025 V:0.5123 A:0.5169 D:0.6110 CAPTAIN NEMO I SAID THIS IS AN IDEAL EASY TO USE WEAPON
2488-130870-0026 V:0.4712 A:0.4695 D:0.5670 I ASK ONLY TO PUT IT TO THE TEST
2488-130870-0027 V:0.5897 A:0.5223 D:0.5995 CONSEIL AND I DID THE SAME BUT NOT WITHOUT HEARING THE CANADIAN TOSS US A SARCASTIC HAPPY HUNTING
2488-130870-0028 V:0.5080 A:0.4578 D:0.5433 ON TOP THE SUIT ENDED IN A COLLAR OF THREADED COPPER ONTO WHICH THE METAL HELMET WAS SCREWED
2488-130870-0029 V:0.5110 A:0.4575 D:0.5323 THREE HOLES PROTECTED BY HEAVY GLASS ALLOWED US TO SEE IN ANY DIRECTION WITH SIMPLY A TURN OF THE HEAD INSIDE THE SPHERE
2488-130870-0030 V:0.6369 A:0.5071 D:0.5865 PLACED ON OUR BACKS THE ROUQUAYROL DEVICE WENT INTO OPERATION AS SOON AS IT WAS IN POSITION AND FOR MY PART I COULD BREATHE WITH EASE
2488-130870-0031 V:0.5807 A:0.5391 D:0.6073 THE RUHMKORFF LAMP HANGING FROM MY BELT MY RIFLE IN HAND I WAS READY TO GO FORTH
2488-130870-0032 V:0.3332 A:0.5442 D:0.6243 BUT IN ALL HONESTY WHILE IMPRISONED IN THESE HEAVY CLOTHES AND NAILED TO THE DECK BY MY LEAD SOLES IT WAS IMPOSSIBLE FOR ME TO TAKE A SINGLE STEP
2488-130870-0033 V:0.5121 A:0.4596 D:0.5574 BUT THIS CIRCUMSTANCE HAD BEEN FORESEEN BECAUSE I FELT MYSELF PROPELLED INTO A LITTLE ROOM ADJOINING THE WARDROBE
2488-130870-0034 V:0.4768 A:0.4293 D:0.5271 TOWED IN THE SAME WAY MY COMPANIONS WENT WITH ME
2488-130870-0035 V:0.4910 A:0.4753 D:0.5593 I HEARD A DOOR WITH WATERTIGHT SEALS CLOSE AFTER US AND WE WERE SURROUNDED BY PROFOUND DARKNESS
2488-130870-0036 V:0.4061 A:0.5253 D:0.6036 AFTER SOME MINUTES A SHARP HISSING REACHED MY EARS
2488-130870-0037 V:0.4399 A:0.4884 D:0.5794 I FELT A DISTINCT SENSATION OF COLD RISING FROM MY FEET TO MY CHEST
2488-130870-0038 V:0.4163 A:0.4811 D:0.5402 APPARENTLY A STOPCOCK INSIDE THE BOAT WAS LETTING IN WATER FROM OUTSIDE WHICH OVERRAN US AND SOON FILLED UP THE ROOM
2488-130870-0039 V:0.5328 A:0.4728 D:0.5557 CONTRIVED IN THE NAUTILUSS SIDE A SECOND DOOR THEN OPENED
2488-130870-0040 V:0.6127 A:0.5487 D:0.6314 WORDS ARE POWERLESS TO DESCRIBE SUCH WONDERS
2488-130870-0041 V:0.5346 A:0.4727 D:0.5623 WHEN EVEN THE PAINTERS BRUSH CANT DEPICT THE EFFECTS UNIQUE TO THE LIQUID ELEMENT HOW CAN THE WRITERS PEN HOPE TO REPRODUCE THEM
2488-130870-0042 V:0.5553 A:0.5011 D:0.5934 ALL THESE OBJECTS LOST A PART OF THEIR WEIGHT EQUAL TO THE WEIGHT OF THE LIQUID THEY DISPLACED AND THANKS TO THIS LAW OF PHYSICS DISCOVERED BY ARCHIMEDES I DID JUST FINE
2488-130870-0043 V:0.5933 A:0.4945 D:0.5884 I WAS NO LONGER AN INERT MASS AND I HAD COMPARATIVELY SPEAKING GREAT FREEDOM OF MOVEMENT
2488-130870-0044 V:0.7210 A:0.5532 D:0.6354 THE SUN ASTONISHED ME WITH ITS POWER
2488-130870-0045 V:0.4584 A:0.4542 D:0.5218 THE SOLAR RAYS EASILY CROSSED THIS AQUEOUS MASS AND DISPERSED ITS DARK COLORS
2488-130870-0046 V:0.6007 A:0.4832 D:0.5618 I COULD EASILY DISTINGUISH OBJECTS ONE HUNDRED METERS AWAY
2488-130870-0047 V:0.5486 A:0.4192 D:0.4984 FARTHER ON THE BOTTOM WAS TINTED WITH FINE SHADES OF ULTRAMARINE THEN OFF IN THE DISTANCE IT TURNED BLUE AND FADED IN THE MIDST OF A HAZY DARKNESS
2488-130870-0048 V:0.6138 A:0.4772 D:0.5651 TRULY THIS WATER SURROUNDING ME WAS JUST A KIND OF AIR DENSER THAN THE ATMOSPHERE ON LAND BUT ALMOST AS TRANSPARENT
2488-130870-0049 V:0.6398 A:0.4677 D:0.5464 ABOVE ME I COULD SEE THE CALM SURFACE OF THE OCEAN
2488-130870-0050 V:0.4674 A:0.4184 D:0.5204 WE WERE WALKING ON SAND THAT WAS FINE GRAINED AND SMOOTH NOT WRINKLED LIKE BEACH SAND WHICH PRESERVES THE IMPRESSIONS LEFT BY THE WAVES
2488-130870-0051 V:0.7077 A:0.5748 D:0.6329 THIS DAZZLING CARPET WAS A REAL MIRROR THROWING BACK THE SUNS RAYS WITH STARTLING INTENSITY
2488-130870-0052 V:0.6611 A:0.5027 D:0.5840 THE OUTCOME AN IMMENSE VISTA OF REFLECTIONS THAT PENETRATED EVERY LIQUID MOLECULE
2488-130870-0053 V:0.5461 A:0.5483 D:0.6103 WILL ANYONE BELIEVE ME IF I ASSERT THAT AT THIS THIRTY FOOT DEPTH I COULD SEE AS IF IT WAS BROAD DAYLIGHT
2488-130870-0054 V:0.6368 A:0.4788 D:0.5845 BUT WHEN NIGHT FELL IN THE MIDST OF THE WATERS THE SHIPS BEACON WOULD SURELY FACILITATE OUR RETURN ON BOARD SINCE ITS RAYS CARRIED WITH PERFECT DISTINCTNESS
2488-130870-0055 V:0.5266 A:0.4221 D:0.4985 MY HANDS PARTED LIQUID CURTAINS THAT CLOSED AGAIN BEHIND ME AND MY FOOTPRINTS FADED SWIFTLY UNDER THE WATERS PRESSURE
2488-130870-0056 V:0.4595 A:0.4108 D:0.4792 SOON SCARCELY BLURRED BY THEIR DISTANCE FROM US THE FORMS OF SOME OBJECTS TOOK SHAPE BEFORE MY EYES
2488-130870-0057 V:0.6736 A:0.5188 D:0.6094 I RECOGNIZED THE LOWER SLOPES OF SOME MAGNIFICENT ROCKS CARPETED BY THE FINEST ZOOPHYTE SPECIMENS AND RIGHT OFF I WAS STRUCK BY AN EFFECT UNIQUE TO THIS MEDIUM
2488-130870-0058 V:0.4492 A:0.3959 D:0.4724 BY THEN IT WAS TEN OCLOCK IN THE MORNING
2488-130870-0059 V:0.5635 A:0.4939 D:0.5522 THE SUNS RAYS HIT THE SURFACE OF THE WAVES AT A FAIRLY OBLIQUE ANGLE DECOMPOSING BY REFRACTION AS THOUGH PASSING THROUGH A PRISM AND WHEN THIS LIGHT CAME IN CONTACT WITH FLOWERS ROCKS BUDS SEASHELLS AND POLYPS THE EDGES OF THESE OBJECTS WERE SHADED WITH ALL SEVEN HUES OF THE SOLAR SPECTRUM
2488-130870-0060 V:0.6915 A:0.5249 D:0.5989 THIS RIOT OF RAINBOW TINTS WAS A WONDER A FEAST FOR THE EYES A GENUINE KALEIDOSCOPE OF RED GREEN YELLOW ORANGE VIOLET INDIGO AND BLUE IN SHORT THE WHOLE PALETTE OF A COLOR HAPPY PAINTER
2488-130870-0061 V:0.6960 A:0.5812 D:0.6468 IF ONLY I HAD BEEN ABLE TO SHARE WITH CONSEIL THE INTENSE SENSATIONS RISING IN MY BRAIN COMPETING WITH HIM IN EXCLAMATIONS OF WONDERMENT
2488-130870-0062 V:0.5390 A:0.5006 D:0.5754 IF ONLY I HAD KNOWN HOW TO EXCHANGE THOUGHTS BY MEANS OF PREARRANGED SIGNAL
2488-130870-0063 V:0.4850 A:0.5022 D:0.5754 S SO FOR LACK OF ANYTHING BETTER I TALKED TO MYSELF I DECLAIMED INSIDE THIS COPPER BOX THAT TOPPED MY HEAD SPENDING MORE AIR ON EMPTY WORDS THAN WAS PERHAPS ADVISABLE
2488-130870-0064 V:0.6501 A:0.4824 D:0.5752 CONSEIL LIKE ME HAD STOPPED BEFORE THIS SPLENDID SIGHT
2488-130870-0065 V:0.4916 A:0.4853 D:0.5894 OBVIOUSLY IN THE PRESENCE OF THESE ZOOPHYTE AND MOLLUSK SPECIMENS THE FINE LAD WAS CLASSIFYING HIS HEAD OFF
2488-130870-0066 V:0.6081 A:0.5195 D:0.5997 VARIOUS ISIS CORAL CORNULARIAN CORAL LIVING IN ISOLATION TUFTS OF VIRGINAL GENUS OCULINA FORMERLY KNOWN BY THE NAME WHITE CORAL PRICKLY FUNGUS CORAL IN THE SHAPE OF MUSHROOMS SEA ANEMONE HOLDING ON BY THEIR MUSCULAR DISKS PROVIDING A LITERAL FLOWERBED ADORNED BY JELLYFISH FROM THE GENUS PORPITA AND STARFISH THAT SPANGLED THE SAND INCLUDING VEINLIKE FEATHER STARS FROM THE GENUS ASTEROPHYTON THAT WERE LIKE FINE LACE EMBROIDERED BY THE HANDS OF WATER NYMPHS THEIR FESTOONS SWAYING TO THE FAINT UNDULATIONS CAUSED BY OUR WALKING
