2488-130870-0068 V:0.4678 A:0.4794 D:0.5545 AND WE WENT FORWARD WHILE OVERHEAD THERE SCUDDED SCHOOLS OF PORTUGUESE MEN OF WAR THAT LET THEIR ULTRAMARINE TENTACLES DRIFT IN THEIR WAKES MEDUSAS WHOSE MILKY WHITE OR DAINTY PINK PARASOLS AND SHADED US FROM THE SUNS RAYS
2488-130870-0069 V:0.6041 A:0.4858 D:0.5587 ALL THESE WONDERS I GLIMPSED IN THE SPACE OF A QUARTER OF A MILE
2488-130870-0070 V:0.4856 A:0.4693 D:0.5536 THEN WE CROSSED A PRAIRIE OF ALGAE OPEN SEA PLANTS THAT THE WATERS HADNT YET TORN LOOSE WHOSE VEGETATION GREW IN WILD PROFUSION
2488-130870-0071 V:0.6269 A:0.5066 D:0.6002 SOFT TO THE FOOT THESE DENSELY TEXTURED LAWNS WOULD HAVE RIVALED THE MOST LUXURIANT CARPETS WOVEN BY THE HAND OF MAN
2488-130870-0072 V:0.3227 A:0.4826 D:0.5611 BUT WHILE THIS GREENERY WAS SPRAWLING UNDER OUR STEPS IT DIDNT NEGLECT US OVERHEAD
2488-130870-0073 V:0.6149 A:0.5186 D:0.5970 THE SURFACE OF THE WATER WAS CRISSCROSSED BY A FLOATING ARBOR OF MARINE PLANTS BELONGING TO THAT SUPERABUNDANT ALGAE FAMILY THAT NUMBERS MORE THAN TW
2488-130870-0076 V:0.7300 A:0.4899 D:0.5963 THESE ALGAE ARE A GENUINE PRODIGY OF CREATION ONE OF THE WONDERS OF WORLD FLORA
2488-130870-0077 V:0.6912 A:0.5262 D:0.6245 THIS FAMILY PRODUCES BOTH THE BIGGEST AND SMALLEST VEGETABLES IN THE WORLD
2488-130870-0078 V:0.6093 A:0.5191 D:0.5934 BECAUSE JUST AS FORTY THOUSAND NEAR INVISIBLE BUDS HAVE BEEN COUNTED IN ONE FIVE SQUARE MILLIMETER SPACE SO ALSO HAVE FUCUS PLANTS BEEN GATHERED THAT WERE OVER FIVE HUNDRED METERS LONG
2488-130870-0079 V:0.3958 A:0.4203 D:0.5248 WE HAD BEEN GONE FROM THE NAUTILUS FOR ABOUT AN HOUR AND A HALF
2488-130870-0080 V:0.4374 A:0.4064 D:0.4624 IT WAS ALMOST NOON
2488-130870-0081 V:0.5441 A:0.4859 D:0.5561 I SPOTTED THIS FACT IN THE PERPENDICULARITY OF THE SUNS RAYS WHICH WERE NO LONGER REFRACTED
2488-130870-0082 V:0.6065 A:0.5502 D:0.5942 BY WHICH POINT WE WERE UNDERGOING A PRESSURE OF TEN ATMOSPHERES
2488-130870-0083 V:0.4752 A:0.5287 D:0.6123 BUT MY DIVING CLOTHES WERE BUILT ALONG SUCH LINES THAT I NEVER SUFFERED FROM THIS PRESSURE
2488-130870-0084 V:0.4129 A:0.4323 D:0.5364 I FELT ONLY A CERTAIN TIGHTNESS IN THE JOINTS OF MY FINGERS AND EVEN THIS DISCOMFORT SOON DISAPPEARED
2488-130870-0085 V:0.4281 A:0.5125 D:0.5943 AS FOR THE EXHAUSTION BOUND TO ACCOMPANY A TWO HOUR STROLL IN SUCH UNFAMILIAR TRAPPINGS IT WAS NIL
2488-130870-0086 V:0.6372 A:0.5151 D:0.5858 HELPED BY THE WATER MY MOVEMENTS WERE EXECUTED WITH STARTLING EASE
2488-130870-0087 V:0.5577 A:0.4969 D:0.5730 ARRIVING AT THIS THREE HUNDRED FOOT DEPTH I STILL DETECTED THE SUNS RAYS BUT JUST BARELY
2488-130870-0088 V:0.4636 A:0.4503 D:0.5253 A MIDPOINT BETWEEN DAY AND NIGHT
2488-130870-0089 V:0.5087 A:0.4727 D:0.5566 BUT WE COULD SEE WELL ENOUGH TO FIND OUR WAY AND IT STILL WASNT NECESSARY TO ACTIVATE THE RUHMKORFF DEVICE
2488-130871-0000 V:0.5438 A:0.3962 D:0.5064 AN UNDERWATER FOREST WE HAD FINALLY ARRIVED ON THE OUTSKIRTS OF THIS FOREST
2488-130871-0001 V:0.4711 A:0.5009 D:0.5598 WHAT OTHER BOLDER PIONEER WOULD COME AX IN HAND TO CLEAR AWAY ITS DARK UNDERBRUSH
2488-130871-0002 V:0.6173 A:0.5098 D:0.6083 THIS FOREST WAS MADE UP OF BIG TREELIKE PLANTS AND WHEN WE ENTERED BENEATH THEIR HUGE ARCHES MY EYES WERE INSTANTLY STRUCK BY THE UNIQUE ARRANGEMENT OF THEIR BRANCHES AN ARRANGEMENT THAT I HAD NEVER BEFORE ENCOUNTERED
2488-130871-0003 V:0.3897 A:0.4482 D:0.5388 NONE OF THE WEEDS CARPETING THE SEAFLOOR NONE OF THE BRANCHES BRISTLING FROM THE SHRUBBERY CREPT OR LEANED OR STRETCHED ON A HORIZONTAL PLANE
2488-130871-0004 V:0.6333 A:0.4906 D:0.5795 THEY ALL ROSE RIGHT UP TOWARD THE SURFACE OF THE OCEAN
2488-130871-0005 V:0.4359 A:0.5042 D:0.5835 EVERY FILAMENT OR RIBBON NO MATTER HOW THIN STOOD RAMROD STRAIGHT
2488-130871-0006 V:0.4913 A:0.5197 D:0.5902 FUCUS PLANTS AND CREEPERS WERE GROWING IN STIFF PERPENDICULAR LINES GOVERNED BY THE DENSITY OF THE ELEMENT THAT GENERATED THEM
2488-130871-0007 V:0.5079 A:0.4552 D:0.5470 LIKEWISE TO THE COMPARATIVE DARKNESS SURROUNDING US
2488-130871-0008 V:0.3811 A:0.4189 D:0.5339 THE SEAFLOOR IN THIS FOREST WAS STREWN WITH SHARP CHUNKS OF STONE THAT WERE HARD TO AVOID
2488-130871-0009 V:0.5871 A:0.4825 D:0.5721 HERE THE RANGE OF UNDERWATER FLORA SEEMED PRETTY COMPREHENSIVE TO ME AS WELL AS MORE ABUNDANT THAN IT MIGHT HAVE BEEN IN THE ARCTIC OR TROPICAL ZONES WHERE SUCH EXHIBITS ARE LESS COMMON
2488-130871-0010 V:0.3428 A:0.5465 D:0.6084 BUT FOR A FEW MINUTES I KEPT ACCIDENTALLY CONFUSING THE TWO KINGDOMS MISTAKING ZOOPHYTES FOR WATER PLANTS
2488-130871-0011 V:0.4997 A:0.4941 D:0.6016 WERE ATTACHED TO THE SEAFLOOR BY ONLY THE MOST MAKESHIFT METHODS
2488-130871-0012 V:0.3666 A:0.5027 D:0.5803 THEY HAD NO ROOTS AND DIDNT CARE WHICH SOLID OBJECTS SECURED THEM SAND SHELLS HUSKS OR PEBBLES THEY DIDNT ASK THEIR HOSTS FOR SUSTENANCE JUST A POINT OF PURCHASE
2488-130871-0013 V:0.5266 A:0.5088 D:0.6033 THESE PLANTS ARE ENTIRELY SELF PROPAGATING AND THE PRINCIPLE OF THEIR EXISTENCE LIES IN THE WATER THAT SUSTAINS AND NOURISHES THEM
2488-130871-0015 V:0.5645 A:0.5052 D:0.5762 BUT NOT YET PRESSED AND DRIED LIKE THE NAUTILUSS SPECIMENS SOME PEACOCKS TAILS SPREAD OPEN LIKE FANS TO STIR UP A COOLING BREEZE SEA TANGLE STRETCHING OUT THEIR YOUNG AND EDIBLE SHOOTS TWISTING STRINGS OF KELP FROM THE GENUS NEREOCYSTIS THAT BLOOMED TO A HEIGHT OF FIFTEEN METERS BOUQUETS OF MERMAIDS CUPS WHOSE STEMS GREW WIDER AT THE TOP AND A NUMBER OF OTHER OPEN SEA PLANTS ALL WITHOUT FLOWERS ITS AN ODD ANOMALY IN THIS BIZARRE ELEMENT
2488-130871-0016 V:0.6003 A:0.5226 D:0.5920 AS ONE WITTY NATURALIST PUTS IT THE ANIMAL KINGDOM BLOSSOMS AND THE VEGETABLE KINGDOM DOESNT
2488-130871-0017 V:0.4956 A:0.5237 D:0.5891 THESE VARIOUS TYPES OF SHRUBBERY WERE AS BIG AS TREES IN THE TEMPERATE ZONES IN THE DAMP SHADE BETWEEN THEM THERE WERE CLUSTERED ACTUAL BUSHES OF MOVING FLOWERS HEDGES OF ZOOPHYTES IN WHICH THERE GREW STONY CORAL STRIPED WITH TWISTING FURROWS YELLOWISH SEA ANEMONE FROM THE GENUS WHILE THERE ROSE UNDERFOOT LIKE A COVEY OF SNIPE YELLOW FISH FROM THE GENUS LEPISOCANTHUS WITH BRISTLING JAWS AND SHARP SCALES FLYING GURNARDS
2488-130871-0018 V:0.4562 A:0.4229 D:0.5264 NEAR ONE OCLOCK CAPTAIN NEMO GAVE THE SIGNAL TO HALT
2488-130871-0019 V:0.6646 A:0.5591 D:0.6368 SPEAKING FOR MYSELF I WAS GLAD TO OBLIGE AND WE STRETCHED OUT BENEATH AN ARBOR OF WINGED KELP WHOSE LONG THIN TENDRILS STOOD UP LIKE ARROWS
2488-130871-0020 V:0.6952 A:0.5402 D:0.6238 I SAW A HAPPY GLEAM IN THE GALLANT LADS EYES AND TO COMMUNICATE HIS PLEASURE IN THE WORLDS SILLIEST WAY
2488-130871-0021 V:0.5074 A:0.5183 D:0.6033 AFTER FOUR HOURS OF STROLLING I WAS QUITE ASTONISHED NOT TO FEEL ANY INTENSE HUNGER
2488-130871-0022 V:0.4673 A:0.5178 D:0.5914 WHAT KEPT MY STOMACH IN SUCH A GOOD MOOD IM UNABLE TO SAY
2488-130871-0023 V:0.4730 A:0.4951 D:0.5865 BUT IN EXCHANGE I EXPERIENCED THAT IRRESISTIBLE DESIRE FOR SLEEP THAT COMES OVER EVERY DIVER
2488-130871-0024 V:0.4502 A:0.4813 D:0.5617 ACCORDINGLY MY EYES SOON CLOSED BEHIND THEIR HEAVY GLASS WINDOWS AND I FELL INTO AN UNCONTROLLABLE DOZE WHICH UNTIL THEN I HAD BEEN ABLE TO FIGHT OFF ONLY THROUGH THE MOVEMENTS OF OUR WALKING
2488-130871-0025 V:0.4843 A:0.4900 D:0.5838 AND I HAD STARTED TO STRETCH MY LIMBS WHEN AN UNEXPECTED APPARITION BROUGHT ME SHARPLY TO MY FEET
2488-130871-0026 V:0.3197 A:0.6598 D:0.7039 A FEW PACES AWAY A MONSTROUS METER HIGH SEA SPIDER WAS STARING AT ME WITH BEADY EYES POISED TO SPRING AT ME
2488-130871-0027 V:0.3594 A:0.5370 D:0.6229 ALTHOUGH MY DIVING SUIT WAS HEAVY ENOUGH TO PROTECT ME FROM THIS ANIMALS BITES I COULDNT KEEP BACK A SHUDDER OF HORROR
2488-130871-0028 V:0.5707 A:0.4793 D:0.5586 JUST THEN CONSEIL WOKE UP TOGETHER WITH THE NAUTILUSS SAILOR
2488-130871-0029 V:0.3163 A:0.4985 D:0.5852 CAPTAIN NEMO ALERTED HIS COMPANION TO THIS HIDEOUS CRUSTACEAN WHICH A SWING OF THE RIFLE BUTT QUICKLY BROUGHT DOWN AND I WATCHED THE MONSTERS HORRIBLE LEGS WRITHING IN DREADFUL CONVULSIONS
2488-130871-0030 V:0.4291 A:0.5300 D:0.6260 THIS ENCOUNTER REMINDED ME THAT OTHER MORE DAUNTING ANIMALS MUST BE LURKING IN THESE DARK REACHES AND MY DIVING SUIT MIGHT NOT BE ADEQUATE PROTECTION AGAINST THEIR ATTACKS
2488-130871-0031 V:0.4078 A:0.5116 D:0.6057 SUCH THOUGHTS HADNT PREVIOUSLY CROSSED MY MIND AND I WAS DETERMINED TO KEEP ON MY GUARD
2488-130871-0032 V:0.4526 A:0.4912 D:0.5723 MEANWHILE I HAD ASSUMED THIS REST PERIOD WOULD BE THE TURNING POINT IN OUR STROLL BUT I WAS MISTAKEN AND INSTEAD OF HEADING BACK TO THE NAUTILUS CAPTAIN NEMO CONTINUED HIS DARING EXCURSION
2488-130871-0033 V:0.5030 A:0.4953 D:0.5731 THE SEAFLOOR KEPT SINKING AND ITS SIGNIFICANTLY STEEPER SLOPE TOOK US TO GREATER DEPTHS
2488-130871-0034 V:0.5035 A:0.5010 D:0.5747 IT MUST HAVE BEEN NEARLY THREE OCLOCK WHEN WE REACHED A NARROW VALLEY GOUGED BETWEEN HIGH VERTICAL WALLS
2488-130871-0035 V:0.6400 A:0.5160 D:0.6059 THANKS TO THE PERFECTION OF OUR EQUIPMENT WE HAD THUS GONE NINETY METERS BELOW THE LIMIT THAT NATURE HAD UNTIL THEN SET ON MANS UNDERWATER EXCURSIONS
2488-130871-0036 V:0.4320 A:0.4636 D:0.5541 NOT A SINGLE OBJECT WAS VISIBLE PAST TEN PACES
2488-130871-0037 V:0.5121 A:0.4919 D:0.5642 CONSEQUENTLY I HAD BEGUN TO GROPE MY WAY WHEN SUDDENLY I SAW THE GLOW OF AN INTENSE WHITE LIGHT
2488-130871-0038 V:0.5432 A:0.5447 D:0.6192 CAPTAIN NEMO HAD JUST ACTIVATED HIS ELECTRIC DEVICE
2488-130871-0039 V:0.5209 A:0.4390 D:0.5386 HIS COMPANION DID LIKEWISE
2488-130871-0040 V:0.5022 A:0.4290 D:0.5162 CONSEIL AND I FOLLOWED SUIT
2488-130871-0041 V:0.5984 A:0.5022 D:0.5668 BY TURNING A SWITCH I ESTABLISHED CONTACT BETWEEN THE INDUCTION COIL AND THE GLASS SPIRAL AND THE SEA LIT UP BY OUR FOUR LANTERNS
2488-130871-0042 V:0.4997 A:0.5206 D:0.6150 I OBSERVED THAT VEGETABLE LIFE WAS DISAPPEARING MORE QUICKLY THAN ANIMAL LIFE
2488-130871-0043 V:0.4506 A:0.4743 D:0.5584 THE OPEN SEA PLANTS HAD ALREADY LEFT BEHIND THE INCREASINGLY ARID SEAFLOOR WHERE A PRODIGIOUS NUMBER OF ANIMALS WERE STILL SWARMING ZOOPHYTES ARTICULATES MOLLUSKS AND FISH
2488-130871-0044 V:0.5847 A:0.4984 D:0.5787 WHILE WE WERE WALKING I THOUGHT THE LIGHTS OF OUR RUHMKORFF DEVICES WOULD AUTOMATICALLY ATTRACT SOME INHABITANTS OF THESE DARK STRATA
2488-130871-0045 V:0.4590 A:0.4525 D:0.5649 BUT IF THEY DID APPROACH US AT LEAST THEY KEPT AT A DISTANCE REGRETTABLE FROM THE HUNTERS STANDPOINT
2488-130871-0046 V:0.4710 A:0.5030 D:0.5778 SEVERAL TIMES I SAW CAPTAIN NEMO STOP AND TAKE AIM WITH HIS RIFLE THEN AFTER SIGHTING DOWN ITS BARREL FOR A FEW SECONDS HE WOULD STRAIGHTEN UP AND RESUME HIS WALK
2488-130871-0047 V:0.5657 A:0.5339 D:0.6053 FINALLY AT AROUND FOUR OCLOCK THIS MARVELOUS EXCURSION CAME TO AN END
2488-130871-0048 V:0.5671 A:0.5161 D:0.5936 A WALL OF SUPERB ROCKS STOOD BEFORE US IMPOSING IN ITS SHEER MASS
2488-130871-0049 V:0.3127 A:0.4385 D:0.5040 THE CAPTAIN STOPPED SUDDENLY
2488-130871-0050 V:0.4606 A:0.5095 D:0.5855 A GESTURE FROM HIM BROUGHT US TO A HALT AND HOWEVER MUCH I WANTED TO CLEAR THIS WALL I HAD TO STOP
2488-130871-0051 V:0.5163 A:0.4224 D:0.5285 HERE ENDED THE DOMAINS OF CAPTAIN NEMO
2488-130871-0052 V:0.3481 A:0.4315 D:0.5183 HE HAD NO DESIRE TO PASS BEYOND THEM
2488-130871-0053 V:0.4081 A:0.4118 D:0.5023 FARTHER ON LAY A PART OF THE GLOBE HE WOULD NO LONGER TREAD UNDERFOOT
2488-130871-0054 V:0.5421 A:0.4957 D:0.5792 OUR RETURN JOURNEY BEGAN
2488-130871-0055 V:0.4155 A:0.4820 D:0.5534 I NOTED THAT WE DIDNT FOLLOW THE SAME PATH IN RETURNING TO THE NAUTILUS
2488-130871-0056 V:0.5105 A:0.4801 D:0.5603 THIS NEW ROUTE VERY STEEP AND HENCE VERY ARDUOUS QUICKLY TOOK US CLOSE TO THE SURFACE OF THE SEA
2488-130871-0057 V:0.3769 A:0.5036 D:0.5928 BUT THIS RETURN TO THE UPPER STRATA WASNT SO SUDDEN THAT DECOMPRESSION TOOK PLACE TOO QUICKLY WHICH COULD HAVE LED TO SERIOUS ORGANIC DISORDERS AND GIVEN US THOSE INTERNAL INJURIES SO FATAL TO DIVERS
2488-130871-0058 V:0.6909 A:0.5190 D:0.5836 WITH GREAT PROMPTNESS THE LIGHT REAPPEARED AND GREW STRONGER AND THE REFRACTION OF THE SUN ALREADY LOW ON THE HORIZON AGAIN RINGED THE EDGES OF VARIOUS OBJECTS WITH THE ENTIRE COLOR SPECTRUM
2488-130871-0059 V:0.5406 A:0.5188 D:0.5927 AT A DEPTH OF TEN METERS WE WALKED AMID A SWARM OF SMALL FISH FROM EVERY SPECIES MORE NUMEROUS THAN BIRDS IN THE AIR MORE AGILE TOO BUT NO AQUATIC GAME WORTHY OF A GUNSHOT HAD YET BEEN OFFERED TO OUR EYES
2488-130871-0060 V:0.4456 A:0.5972 D:0.6520 JUST THEN I SAW THE CAPTAINS WEAPON SPRING TO HIS SHOULDER AND TRACK A MOVING OBJECT THROUGH THE BUSHES
2488-130871-0061 V:0.4145 A:0.5513 D:0.6042 A SHOT WENT OFF I HEARD A FAINT HISSING AND AN ANIMAL DROPPED A FEW PACES AWAY LITERALLY STRUCK BY LIGHTNING
2488-130871-0062 V:0.8578 A:0.6018 D:0.6896 IT WAS A MAGNIFICENT SEA OTTER FROM THE GENUS ENHYDRA
2488-130871-0063 V:0.3619 A:0.4880 D:0.5929 HUNTED AND TRAPPED BY FISHERMEN THIS VALUABLE CARNIVORE HAS BECOME EXTREMELY RARE AND IT TAKES REFUGE CHIEFLY IN THE NORTHERNMOST PARTS OF THE PACIFIC WHERE IN ALL LIKELIHOOD ITS SPECIES WILL SOON BE FACING EXTINCTION
2488-130871-0064 V:0.5275 A:0.4886 D:0.5848 CAPTAIN NEMOS COMPANION PICKED UP THE ANIMAL LOADED IT ON HIS SHOULDER AND WE TOOK TO THE TRAIL AGAIN
2488-130871-0065 V:0.3759 A:0.4265 D:0.5133 FOR AN HOUR PLAINS OF SAND UNROLLED BEFORE OUR STEPS
2488-130871-0066 V:0.4793 A:0.4619 D:0.5308 OFTEN THE SEAFLOOR ROSE TO WITHIN TWO METERS OF THE SURFACE OF THE WATER
2488-130871-0067 V:0.6120 A:0.5023 D:0.5766 I COULD THEN SEE OUR IMAGES CLEARLY MIRRORED ON THE UNDERSIDE OF THE WAVES BUT REFLECTED UPSIDE DOWN ABOVE US THERE APPEARED AN IDENTICAL BAND THAT DUPLICATED OUR EVERY MOVEMENT AND GESTURE IN SHORT A PERFECT LIKENESS OF THE QUARTET NEAR WHICH IT WALKED BUT WITH HEADS DOWN AND FEET IN THE AIR
2488-130871-0068 V:0.4916 A:0.4838 D:0.5665 ANOTHER UNUSUAL EFFECT
2488-130871-0069 V:0.4951 A:0.4160 D:0.4866 HEAVY CLOUDS PASSED ABOVE US FORMING AND FADING SWIFTLY BUT AFTER THINKING IT OVER
2488-130871-0070 V:0.5327 A:0.4571 D:0.5513 SWIFTLY SKIMMING THE SURFACE OF THE SEA
2488-130871-0071 V:0.6072 A:0.5473 D:0.6562 ON THIS OCCASION I WITNESSED ONE OF THE FINEST GUNSHOTS EVER TO THRILL THE MARROW OF A HUNTER
2488-130871-0072 V:0.5085 A:0.4698 D:0.5528 QUITE CLEARLY VISIBLE APPROACHED AND HOVERED OVER US
2488-130871-0073 V:0.5682 A:0.5830 D:0.6421 WHEN IT WAS JUST A FEW METERS ABOVE THE WAVES CAPTAIN NEMOS COMPANION TOOK AIM AND FIRED
2488-130871-0074 V:0.5536 A:0.5046 D:0.5859 THE ANIMAL DROPPED ELECTROCUTED AND ITS DESCENT BROUGHT IT WITHIN REACH OF OUR ADROIT HUNTER WHO PROMPTLY TOOK POSSESSION OF IT
2488-130871-0075 V:0.7638 A:0.5191 D:0.6273 IT WAS AN ALBATROSS OF THE FINEST SPECIES A WONDERFUL SPECIMEN OF THESE OPEN SEA FOWL
2488-130871-0076 V:0.3540 A:0.4299 D:0.5347 THIS INCIDENT DID NOT INTERRUPT OUR WALK
2488-130871-0077 V:0.4153 A:0.4217 D:0.5118 FOR TWO HOURS WE WERE SOMETIMES LED OVER PLAINS OF SAND SOMETIMES OVER PRAIRIES OF SEAWEED THAT WERE QUITE ARDUOUS TO CROSS
2488-130871-0078 V:0.3576 A:0.4718 D:0.5542 IN ALL HONESTY I WAS DEAD TIRED BY THE TIME I SPOTTED A HAZY GLOW HALF A MILE AWAY CUTTING THROUGH THE DARKNESS OF THE WATERS
2488-130871-0079 V:0.4962 A:0.3905 D:0.4799 IT WAS THE NAUTILUSS BEACON
2488-130871-0080 V:0.6049 A:0.5698 D:0.6214 WITHIN TWENTY MINUTES WE WOULD BE ON BOARD AND THERE I COULD BREATHE EASY AGAIN BECAUSE MY TANKS CURRENT AIR SUPPLY SEEMED TO BE QUITE LOW IN OXYGEN
2488-130871-0081 V:0.4515 A:0.4715 D:0.5505 BUT I WAS RECKONING WITHOUT AN ENCOUNTER THAT SLIGHTLY DELAYED OUR ARRIVAL
2488-130871-0082 V:0.3473 A:0.4894 D:0.5870 I WAS LAGGING BEHIND SOME TWENTY PACES
2488-130871-0083 V:0.4581 A:0.5544 D:0.6386 WITH HIS POWERFUL HANDS HE SENT ME BUCKLING TO THE GROUND WHILE HIS COMPANION DID THE SAME TO CONSEIL
2488-130871-0084 V:0.3277 A:0.5404 D:0.6131 AT FIRST I DIDNT KNOW WHAT TO MAKE OF THIS SUDDEN ASSAULT BUT I WAS REASSURED TO OBSERVE THE CAPTAIN LYING MOTIONLESS BESIDE ME
2488-130871-0085 V:0.5162 A:0.5625 D:0.6300 I WAS STRETCHED OUT ON THE SEAFLOOR DIRECTLY BENEATH SOME BUSHES OF ALGAE WHEN I RAISED MY HEAD AND SPIED TWO ENORMOUS MASSES HURTLING BY THROWING OFF PHOSPHORESCENT GLIMMERS
2488-130871-0086 V:0.2361 A:0.5551 D:0.6401 MY BLOOD TURNED COLD IN MY VEINS
2488-130871-0087 V:0.3279 A:0.5507 D:0.6349 I SAW THAT WE WERE UNDER THREAT FROM A FEARSOME PAIR OF SHARKS
2488-130871-0088 V:0.4991 A:0.6011 D:0.6602 THEY WERE BLUE SHARKS DULL GLASSY STARES AND PHOSPHORESCENT MATTER OOZING FROM HOLES AROUND THEIR SNOUTS
2488-130871-0089 V:0.3522 A:0.5593 D:0.6452 THEY WERE LIKE MONSTROUS FIREFLIES THAT COULD THOROUGHLY PULVERIZE A MAN IN THEIR IRON JAWS
2488-130871-0091 V:0.2229 A:0.4898 D:0.5999 LUCKILY THESE VORACIOUS ANIMALS HAVE POOR EYESIGHT
2488-130871-0092 V:0.4799 A:0.5159 D:0.6040 GRAZING US WITH THEIR BROWNISH FINS AND MIRACULOUSLY WE ESCAPED A DANGER GREATER THAN ENCOUNTERING A TIGER DEEP IN THE JUNGLE
2488-130871-0093 V:0.5726 A:0.5166 D:0.5851 HALF AN HOUR LATER GUIDED BY ITS ELECTRIC TRAIL WE REACHED THE NAUTILUS
2488-130871-0094 V:0.4790 A:0.4986 D:0.5489 THEN HE PRESSED A BUTTON
2488-130871-0095 V:0.4532 A:0.5412 D:0.5997 I HEARD PUMPS OPERATING WITHIN THE SHIP I FELT THE WATER LOWERING AROUND ME AND IN A FEW MOMENTS THE CELL WAS COMPLETELY EMPTY
2488-130871-0096 V:0.4968 A:0.4896 D:0.5604 THE INSIDE DOOR OPENED AND WE PASSED INTO THE WARDROBE
2488-130871-0097 V:0.4147 A:0.4519 D:0.5422 THERE OUR DIVING SUITS WERE REMOVED NOT WITHOUT DIFFICULTY
2488-36616-0001 V:0.4523 A:0.4215 D:0.4944 THIS MYSTERY PUZZLED ME
2488-36616-0002 V:0.5175 A:0.4457 D:0.5353 FINDING IT IMPOSSIBLE TO FORM ANY VIEWS I DRIFTED FROM ONE EXTREME TO THE OTHER
2488-36616-0003 V:0.3965 A:0.3957 D:0.5158 SOMETHING WAS OUT THERE THAT MUCH WAS CERTAIN AND ANY DOUBTING THOMAS WAS INVITED TO PLACE HIS FINGER ON THE SCOTIAS WOUND
2488-36616-0004 V:0.5512 A:0.4030 D:0.4928 WHEN I ARRIVED IN NEW YORK
2488-36616-0005 V:0.5138 A:0.5216 D:0.5976 ALSO DISCREDITED WAS THE IDEA OF A FLOATING HULL OR SOME OTHER ENORMOUS WRECKAGE AND AGAIN BECAUSE OF THIS SPEED OF MOVEMENT
2488-36616-0006 V:0.5017 A:0.4287 D:0.5296 SO ONLY TWO POSSIBLE SOLUTIONS TO THE QUESTION WERE LEFT CREATING TWO VERY DISTINCT GROUPS OF SUPPORTERS
2488-36616-0007 V:0.4630 A:0.4427 D:0.5322 IT COULDNT STAND UP TO INQUIRIES CONDUCTED IN BOTH THE NEW WORLD AND THE OLD
2488-36616-0008 V:0.4304 A:0.4529 D:0.5535 THAT A PRIVATE INDIVIDUAL HAD SUCH A MECHANISM AT HIS DISPOSAL WAS LESS THAN PROBABLE
2488-36616-0009 V:0.4921 A:0.4271 D:0.4981 WHERE AND WHEN HAD HE BUILT IT AND HOW COULD HE HAVE BUILT IT IN SECRET
2488-36616-0010 V:0.4146 A:0.4774 D:0.5766 ONLY SOME GOVERNMENT COULD OWN SUCH AN ENGINE OF DESTRUCTION AND IN THESE DISASTER FILLED TIMES WHEN MEN TAX THEIR INGENUITY TO BUILD INCREASINGLY POWERFUL AGGRESSIVE WEAPONS IT WAS POSSIBLE THAT UNKNOWN TO THE REST OF THE WORLD SOME NATION COULD HAVE BEEN TESTING SUCH A FEARSOME MACHINE
2488-36616-0011 V:0.3836 A:0.4468 D:0.5241 AND THE TORPEDO HAS LED TO THIS UNDERWATER BATTERING RAM WHICH IN TURN WILL LEAD TO THE WORLD PUTTING ITS FOOT DOWN
2488-36616-0012 V:0.4776 A:0.2916 D:0.3902 AT LEAST I HOPE IT WILL
